{"items":[{"id":"AR-001","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"easy","topic":"percent","stem":"A jacket priced at $80 is discounted 25%, then taxed at 8%. What is the final price?","choices":["A) $64.00","B) $64.80","C) $68.40","D) $86.40","E) $60.00"],"answer":"B","explanation":"25% off $80 = $60. Tax 8% of $60 = $4.80. Total $64.80."},{"id":"AR-002","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"distance-rate-time","stem":"A truck travels 150 miles at 50 mph and returns the same 150 miles at 75 mph. What is the average speed for the round trip?","choices":["A) 60 mph","B) 62.5 mph","C) 65 mph","D) 66.7 mph","E) 70 mph"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Time out = 3 h, time back = 2 h, total 5 h for 300 miles. 300/5 = 60 mph. Not the mean of 50 and 75."},{"id":"AR-003","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"work-rate","stem":"Pipe A fills a tank in 6 hours. Pipe B fills it in 3 hours. If both run together, how long to fill the tank?","choices":["A) 1 hour","B) 1.5 hours","C) 2 hours","D) 4.5 hours","E) 9 hours"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Rates 1/6 + 1/3 = 1/6 + 2/6 = 3/6 = 1/2 tank per hour → 2 hours."},{"id":"AR-004","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"ratio","stem":"A fuel blend uses jet fuel and additive in the ratio 9:1. How many gallons of additive are in 40 gallons of blend?","choices":["A) 3","B) 4","C) 4.5","D) 9","E) 36"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Parts = 10. Additive = 1/10 of 40 = 4 gallons."},{"id":"AR-005","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"hard","topic":"mixture","stem":"8 liters of a 20% saline solution are mixed with 2 liters of a 70% saline solution. What is the percent saline in the mixture?","choices":["A) 30%","B) 32%","C) 36%","D) 45%","E) 50%"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Salt: 0.20*8 + 0.70*2 = 1.6 + 1.4 = 3.0 liters salt in 10 liters → 30%."},{"id":"AR-006","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"interest","stem":"Simple interest on $2,000 at 6% per year for 18 months is","choices":["A) $120","B) $180","C) $216","D) $240","E) $1,800"],"answer":"B","explanation":"t = 1.5 years. I = 2000 * 0.06 * 1.5 = 180."},{"id":"AR-007","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"unit-conversion","stem":"A runner covers 2.5 miles. How many feet is that? (1 mile = 5280 feet)","choices":["A) 10,560","B) 12,000","C) 13,200","D) 15,840","E) 26,400"],"answer":"C","explanation":"2.5 * 5280 = 13,200."},{"id":"AR-008","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"hard","topic":"work-rate","stem":"A crew of 4 finishes a job in 9 hours. Assuming equal rates, how many hours would a crew of 6 take?","choices":["A) 4","B) 5","C) 6","D) 7","E) 13.5"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Total person-hours = 36. 36/6 = 6 hours."},{"id":"AR-009","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"easy","topic":"percent-change","stem":"A drone inventory goes from 40 to 50. The percent increase is","choices":["A) 10%","B) 20%","C) 25%","D) 80%","E) 125%"],"answer":"C","explanation":"(10/40)*100 = 25%."},{"id":"AR-010","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"hard","topic":"distance-rate-time","stem":"Two aircraft leave the same field at the same time, flying opposite directions at 180 mph and 220 mph. After how many hours are they 1,000 miles apart?","choices":["A) 2.0","B) 2.5","C) 2.75","D) 3.0","E) 4.0"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Closing speed 400 mph. 1000/400 = 2.5 hours."},{"id":"MK-001","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"easy","topic":"algebra","stem":"Solve: 3x − 7 = 11","choices":["A) 4","B) 5","C) 6","D) 18/3","E) −6"],"answer":"C","explanation":"3x = 18, x = 6."},{"id":"MK-002","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"exponents","stem":"Simplify: (2^3)^2 × 2^2","choices":["A) 2^6","B) 2^7","C) 2^8","D) 2^12","E) 64"],"answer":"C","explanation":"(2^3)^2 = 2^6. 2^6 × 2^2 = 2^8."},{"id":"MK-003","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"geometry-triangle","stem":"A right triangle has legs 6 and 8. The hypotenuse is","choices":["A) 7","B) 9","C) 10","D) 14","E) 48"],"answer":"C","explanation":"6-8-10 is a scaled 3-4-5 triangle. 36+64=100."},{"id":"MK-004","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"special-right","stem":"In a 30-60-90 triangle the short leg is 5. The hypotenuse is","choices":["A) 5√2","B) 5√3","C) 10","D) 15","E) 10√3"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Hypotenuse = 2 × short leg = 10."},{"id":"MK-005","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"slope","stem":"Slope of the line through (2, 3) and (6, 11) is","choices":["A) 1","B) 2","C) 3","D) 4","E) 8/4"],"answer":"B","explanation":"(11-3)/(6-2) = 8/4 = 2."},{"id":"MK-006","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"hard","topic":"quadratic","stem":"Solutions of x^2 − 5x + 6 = 0 are","choices":["A) −2 and −3","B) 2 and 3","C) 1 and 6","D) −1 and 6","E) 0 and 5"],"answer":"B","explanation":"(x-2)(x-3)=0."},{"id":"MK-007","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"circle","stem":"Area of a circle with diameter 10 is","choices":["A) 10π","B) 20π","C) 25π","D) 100π","E) 5π"],"answer":"C","explanation":"r=5, A=πr^2=25π."},{"id":"MK-008","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"inequality","stem":"Solve: −2x + 4 > 10","choices":["A) x > −3","B) x < −3","C) x > 3","D) x < 3","E) x > −7"],"answer":"B","explanation":"−2x > 6. Divide by −2 and flip: x < −3."},{"id":"MK-009","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"hard","topic":"volume","stem":"A cylinder has radius 3 and height 4. Volume in terms of π is","choices":["A) 12π","B) 24π","C) 36π","D) 48π","E) 144π"],"answer":"C","explanation":"V=πr^2h=π*9*4=36π."},{"id":"MK-010","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"easy","topic":"fractions","stem":"(3/4) ÷ (1/8) =","choices":["A) 3/32","B) 3/2","C) 6","D) 8/3","E) 24"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Multiply by 8/1: 24/4 = 6."},{"id":"MK-011","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"absolute-value","stem":"|x − 4| = 7 has solutions","choices":["A) 11 only","B) −3 only","C) 11 and −3","D) 4 and 7","E) no real solution"],"answer":"C","explanation":"x−4=7 or x−4=−7 → x=11 or x=−3."},{"id":"MK-012","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"hard","topic":"coordinate","stem":"Distance between (0, 0) and (5, 12) is","choices":["A) 7","B) 13","C) 17","D) 60","E) √17"],"answer":"B","explanation":"√(25+144)=√169=13."},{"id":"MK-013","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"exponents","stem":"Simplify: 3^0 + 3^2 + 3^(-1)","choices":["A) 9.5","B) 10","C) 10 1/3","D) 13","E) 12"],"answer":"C","explanation":"3^0=1, 3^2=9, 3^(-1)=1/3. Sum = 10 1/3."},{"id":"MK-014","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"percent-as-decimal","stem":"Which is equivalent to 0.045?","choices":["A) 45%","B) 4.5%","C) 0.45%","D) 450%","E) 4/5"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Move the decimal two places: 0.045 = 4.5%."},{"id":"MK-015","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"hard","topic":"special-right","stem":"A 45-45-90 triangle has a hypotenuse of 10. Each leg is","choices":["A) 5","B) 5√2","C) 10√2","D) 5√3","E) 20"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Legs are hypotenuse / √2 = 10/√2 = 5√2."},{"id":"MK-016","subtest":"math_knowledge","difficulty":"medium","topic":"systems","stem":"If 2x + y = 11 and x − y = 1, then x equals","choices":["A) 3","B) 4","C) 5","D) 6","E) 10"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Add the equations: 3x = 12, x = 4."},{"id":"AR-011","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"percent","stem":"A server rack draws 1.2 kW. After efficiency work it draws 15% less. New draw?","choices":["A) 0.18 kW","B) 1.02 kW","C) 1.05 kW","D) 1.35 kW","E) 1.38 kW"],"answer":"B","explanation":"15% of 1.2 = 0.18. 1.2 − 0.18 = 1.02 kW."},{"id":"AR-012","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"hard","topic":"work-rate","stem":"Script A finishes a job in 40 minutes. Script B finishes it in 60 minutes. Running together, how many minutes to finish?","choices":["A) 20","B) 24","C) 25","D) 50","E) 100"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Rates 1/40 + 1/60 = 3/120 + 2/120 = 5/120 = 1/24. Time = 24 minutes."},{"id":"AR-013","subtest":"arithmetic_reasoning","difficulty":"medium","topic":"ratio","stem":"A team of 8 analysts and 2 developers is scaled to keep the same ratio at 40 people. How many developers?","choices":["A) 4","B) 8","C) 10","D) 16","E) 32"],"answer":"B","explanation":"8:2 = 4:1. 5 parts → 40/5=8 per part. Developers = 1 part = 8."}]}
